# Architecture Guidelines

## Scene hierarchy rules
- PachinkoBoard owns all board elements and spheres
- Sphere is RigidBody2D — never move it manually, only apply impulses
- Board elements (Pin, Bumper, Pocket) are StaticBody2D or Area2D
- GameManager orchestrates round flow — it does NOT contain gameplay logic
- UI scenes are purely visual — they read from GameState via signals, never mutate it

## Autoloads (global singletons)
- `SignalBus` — only signal declarations, no logic
- `GameState` — mutable global state, no UI logic
- Never add new autoloads without strong justification

## Resource types
- `PlayerData` extends Resource — serialize player state
- `BoardLayout` extends Resource — defines predefined element slot positions
- `BoardElement` extends Resource — type, level, special properties

## Folder structure
res://
├── autoload/ SignalBus.gd, GameState.gd
├── scenes/
│ ├── game/ GameManager.tscn, RoundManager.tscn
│ ├── pachinko/ PachinkoBoard.tscn, Sphere.tscn, Pin.tscn, Bumper.tscn, Pocket.tscn
│ ├── ui/ HUD.tscn, Shop.tscn, Inventory.tscn, BoardEditor.tscn
│ └── minigames/ WheelOfFortune.tscn, SlotDrums.tscn
├── scripts/ Pure logic classes (no Node inheritance)
│ SphereLogic.gd, DevilsGaze.gd, QuotaSystem.gd, MergeSystem.gd, BonusGameQueue.gd
├── resources/ PlayerData.gd, BoardLayout.gd, BoardElement.gd
├── assets/
│ ├── sprites/
│ ├── shaders/ ps1_dither.gdshader, crt_overlay.gdshader
│ ├── sounds/
│ └── fonts/
└── addons/


## DO NOT
- Do not put game logic in UI scripts
- Do not reference scenes by path string — use preload()
- Do not use yield() — use await signal instead
- Do not generate .tscn files — always create scenes manually in Godot Editor